00:41:49.910 --> 00:41:50.190
Okay.

00:41:50.350 --> 00:41:55.410
It's cold out there.

00:41:55.430 --> 00:41:56.310
We want to keep you warm.

00:41:56.430 --> 00:41:57.500
Take that.

00:41:57.680 --> 00:41:58.060
Thank you.

00:41:58.180 --> 00:41:59.460
Are you okay?

00:42:09.084 --> 00:42:10.084
I'll get you off.

00:42:34.890 --> 00:42:35.760
Oh, you're reading already?

00:42:35.940 --> 00:42:37.960
I thought maybe I could read you a story.

00:42:39.500 --> 00:42:40.560
I'm right at the good part.

00:42:41.060 --> 00:42:41.560
Oh, I understand.

00:42:41.840 --> 00:42:44.970
But you can read over my shoulder if you want.

00:42:45.000 --> 00:42:49.860
want oh that's okay if you're in the thick of it i just like it when we read together sometimes lately

00:43:00.028 --> 00:43:02.028
I've been wishing that you had an older sister.

00:43:02.364 --> 00:43:04.364
Because you're coming to an age where...

00:43:05.244 --> 00:43:07.324
There are so many things you're going to want to know.

00:43:09.308 --> 00:43:11.548
I'm probably not the person you're going to want to ask.

00:43:13.180 --> 00:43:15.300
I know it's hard because sometimes you feel...

00:43:16.860 --> 00:43:19.500
more comfortable telling things to a mom

00:43:19.708 --> 00:43:20.548
than you would feel.

00:43:21.628 --> 00:43:22.668
telling him to a dad.

00:43:24.700 --> 00:43:25.500
But...

00:43:27.516 --> 00:43:28.516
I want you to.

00:43:28.700 --> 00:43:29.660
Try and tell me.

00:43:31.400 --> 00:43:36.570
And I'll do my best to help you the way that mom would have.

00:43:39.100 --> 00:43:43.540
Who knows? Maybe it'll get easier for both of us.

00:43:45.360 --> 00:43:48.610
You're doing okay, Dad, except for the braids.

00:43:50.820 --> 00:43:51.180
Thanks, sweetie.

00:43:53.660 --> 00:43:56.840
Wait, Dad?

00:44:02.400 --> 00:44:03.500
We could read this book.

00:44:04.570 --> 00:44:05.910
Read that a million times already.

00:44:07.160 --> 00:44:08.540
But you've only read it to me.

00:44:09.200 --> 00:44:10.740
What if I read it to you this time?

00:44:22.920 --> 00:44:26.520
The unicorn lived in a lilac wood, and she lived all alone.

00:44:27.120 --> 00:44:29.420
She was very old, though she did not know it.

00:44:30.350 --> 00:44:33.630
And she was no longer the careless color of sea foam,

00:44:34.480 --> 00:44:37.340
but rather the color of snow falling on the moonlit night.

00:44:37.340 --> 00:44:41.350
But her eyes were still clear and unwearied,

00:44:41.430 --> 00:44:44.460
and she still moved like a shadow on the sea.

00:45:26.650 --> 00:45:29.440
Father, I have sinned.
